\pard\sa200\sl276\slmult1\par
# ABSTRACT\par
\par
Linux is one of the most widely used operating-system platforms in modern computing. It is extensively used in servers, cloud infrastructure, networking systems, embedded devices, software-development environments, cybersecurity, data centers, and high-performance computing.\par
\par
This course was designed to provide **Neil Vikram Khare** with a comprehensive understanding of the Linux operating system and its practical command-line environment. The major areas covered during the course were **Linux Fundamentals, Linux Operating System, Linux Administration, Linux Command Line, and Shell/Bash**.\par
\par
The course combined theoretical learning with practical activities. It introduced the structure and architecture of Linux, the Linux file system, users and groups, file permissions, processes, services, storage, networking, software packages, and system monitoring.\par
\par
The command-line component focused on the practical use of Linux commands for navigating the file system, creating and managing files, searching information, monitoring processes, examining system resources, managing permissions, and performing basic administrative tasks.\par
\par
The Shell/Bash component introduced scripting and automation. Topics such as variables, input and output, conditional statements, loops, functions, pipes, redirection, and script execution were studied.\par
\par
Practical activities were included throughout the course to reinforce theoretical concepts. Screenshots of relevant Linux terminal activities can be inserted in the designated sections of this report as evidence of practical work.\par
\par
