# 36. APPLICATIONS OF LINUX\par
\par
Linux is used in a wide range of technological environments.\par
\par
## Web Servers\par
\par
Linux is widely used to host websites and web applications.\par
\par
## Cloud Computing\par
\par
Linux is extensively used for cloud virtual machines, containers, and infrastructure services.\par
\par
## Cybersecurity\par
\par
Linux environments are widely used for security research, defensive security, system monitoring, digital analysis, and security testing.\par
\par
## Software Development\par
\par
Developers use Linux for programming, compilation, version control, application deployment, and automation.\par
\par
## Networking\par
\par
Linux can be used in network infrastructure, routing, monitoring, and network services.\par
\par
## Embedded Systems\par
\par
Linux has been adapted for embedded devices and specialized computing systems.\par
\par
## High-Performance Computing\par
\par
Linux is commonly used in high-performance computing and research environments.\par
