\par
The Linux Operating System course provided **Neil Vikram Khare** with a structured understanding of Linux fundamentals, system architecture, administration, command-line operations, and Shell/Bash scripting.\par
\par
The course began with fundamental concepts such as Linux distributions, the kernel, system architecture, and the Linux file-system hierarchy. These concepts established the foundation required to understand how Linux systems operate.\par
\par
The Linux Administration component introduced important administrative tasks including user and group management, file permissions, process management, storage monitoring, package management, service management, networking, and system monitoring.\par
\par
The Linux Command Line component provided practical knowledge of interacting with the operating system through terminal commands. File and directory management, searching, process monitoring, system inspection, networking, pipes, and redirection demonstrated the flexibility of the Linux CLI.\par
\par
The Shell/Bash component introduced scripting and automation. Variables, user input, conditional statements, loops, functions, and command execution demonstrated how routine operations can be organized into reusable scripts.\par
\par
The practical activities strengthened the theoretical knowledge by allowing direct interaction with Linux systems. The screenshots included in the practical documentation section provide space for recording evidence of these activities.\par
\par
Overall, the course established a strong foundation in **Linux Fundamentals, Linux Operating System, Linux Administration, Linux Command Line, and Shell/Bash**. These skills provide a useful base for further learning in areas such as **system administration, networking, cloud computing, DevOps, software development, and cybersecurity**.\par
